  <h1>Entropy &amp; the Phases of Integration</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">The one law that knows which way time runs &mdash; and the order's reading of what
  it is counting. Written in two registers, with the join between them marked on every paragraph.</p>
</section>

<!-- ============================== THE PREMISE ============================= -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Begin Here &mdash; and read this paragraph before any other</p>
    <h2 id="t-two-registers-one-page">Two Registers, One Page</h2>
    <p class="lede">The thermodynamics on this page is standard and settled. The doctrine on this page is
    the order's own, is filed as myth, and should not be cited as physics by anyone, including us.</p>

    <p>This is the companion page to <a href="/moebius-seam/">the Moebius Seam</a> and is built the same
    way. First the measured account: what entropy is, why heat flows one way, what a phase of matter
    actually is, and where information and thermodynamics turn out to be the same subject. Then the
    order's teaching: that <strong>phases of heat and matter are phases of integration</strong> of other
    things inside a collapsed memory; that the polarity of proton against electron, and therefore
    electromagnetism, is what integration looks like from inside; that these phased states stand at
    different <em>levels</em> of integration; that existence is observed by the
    <strong>spiral being</strong> on its positively polarised journey from nothing towards infinity, alpha
    and omega; and that the Seam follows the flow at the point of waveform collapse between the poles.</p>

    <p>Then the numbers &mdash; the further poles at <strong>101</strong> and <strong>666</strong>, the
    deflection off <strong>999</strong>, and the reverberation between 666 and 333 that continues until the
    observed being can at last pass 999 and go on towards infinity. And then, as always, the section that
    sets out how all of it could be wrong.</p>

    <p class="muted small">Grading throughout: <span class="sci">&#9670; established science</span> &middot;
    <span class="hist">&#9670; scholarship and history</span> &middot;
    <span class="spec">&#9670; speculative and contested</span> &middot;
    <span class="myth">&#9670; myth, tradition and primary esoteric text</span>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

