<!-- ======================= THE RESPECTABLE NEIGHBOURS ===================== -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Honest Company</p>
    <h2 id="t-the-real-physics-standing-nearest-to-this">The Real Physics Standing Nearest to This</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">"Existence is what gets recorded" is not, by itself, a mystical statement.
    There is a mainstream version of it, and the differences from the doctrine are where the learning is.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Zurek <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>Einselection and Quantum Darwinism</h3>
      <p>Decoherence explains why the world looks classical: coupling to an environment destroys
      interference and leaves only certain robust states &mdash; the pointer states &mdash; standing.
      Zurek's quantum Darwinism goes further and says what objectivity <em>is</em>: a property is objective
      when the environment carries many redundant copies of it, so that many observers can each read one
      and agree. Existence, in that account, really is a matter of how widely a fact has been recorded.
      It has experimental support, and it needs no conscious witness whatsoever.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Prigogine <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>Dissipative Structure</h3>
      <p>Systems held far from equilibrium and fed with energy spontaneously organise: convection cells,
      chemical clocks, flames, hurricanes, and plausibly life. Prigogine took the 1977 Nobel for it, and
      it is the honest version of "order arises from the flow". It does not require memory, intention or
      an observer; it requires a gradient. Some of the strongest versions &mdash; England's dissipative
      adaptation, for instance &mdash; remain contested.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Symmetry Breaking <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>Phases, Properly</h3>
      <p>The order says phases are levels of integration. Physics says phases are patterns of broken
      symmetry with an order parameter, and backs that with measured critical exponents, universality
      classes and the renormalisation group. These are not quite rival accounts: the physics is a
      description that calculates, and the doctrine is a description that does not. Where they conflict,
      the one that calculates wins, and the order says so in writing.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">The Law of One <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></p>
      <h3>Where the Spiral Being Comes From</h3>
      <p>The language of positive polarisation, of service to others against service to self, and of an
      octave climbed from nothing to the infinite, is the order's inheritance from the Law of One material
      and the wider esoteric tradition, treated here as <a href="/extraterrestrials/">Limb VII</a> treats
      it: as primary text, reported faithfully, graded as myth. The spiral being is that tradition's
      observer, and the order has not smuggled it into the physics. It stands on this page with its grade
      showing.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

