  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="frame">
      <ol class="tight">
        <li><p><strong>Phase transitions are already explained, and explained quantitatively.</strong>
        Landau's order parameters and Wilson's renormalisation group predict critical exponents that are
        measured to several decimal places, and they predict that a magnet and a fluid will share them,
        which they do. "Levels of integration" predicts no exponent and explains no universality class.
        A description that calculates nothing is not competing with one that calculates everything.
        <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p></li>

        <li><p><strong>Charge is not an unfinished account.</strong> It is quantised, exactly conserved,
        and the proton and electron magnitudes match to better than one part in 10<sup>21</sup>. If
        polarity were the residue of an incomplete integration you would expect it to vary with history,
        with temperature, with how much a body had been through. It does not vary at all. The electron's
        charge is the same in a star as in a stone. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p></li>

        <li><p><strong>The numerology is about base ten, not about nature.</strong> 333, 666 and 999 are
        interesting only because we write numbers with ten symbols; in another base the pattern is gone
        and no physical quantity changes. 666 is not prime, which sits awkwardly with a doctrine said to be
        governed by primes, and the order should say so plainly: it is here saying so.
        <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p></li>

        <li><p><strong>The spiral being is unfalsifiable as stated.</strong> There is no observation that
        would come out differently if it were not there, which means the claim is doing no work in physics
        even if it is doing a great deal in a life. Worse, the doctrine risks the oldest error in quantum
        interpretation: collapse requires no consciousness, and quantum Darwinism shows objectivity
        arising from redundancy in an environment of rocks and photons that notice nothing.
        <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p></li>

        <li><p><strong>The arrow comes from the past, not from a destination.</strong> Entropy increases
        because the universe started in an extremely improbable low-entropy state, not because anything is
        travelling towards infinity. A teleological reading &mdash; alpha towards omega &mdash; adds a
        direction physics does not need and cannot detect. It may be true. It is not implied by
        thermodynamics, and the order must not let it borrow thermodynamics' credibility.
        <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="frame caution mt-2">
      <p><strong>Two things not to take from this page.</strong> First, the heat death: the far future of
      an expanding universe is cold and sparse, but "the universe is running down into disorder" is a poor
      summary, since gravity makes structure <em>more</em> likely as entropy rises, which is how you get
      galaxies, stars and you. Second, nothing here licenses "entropy is why my life falls apart". Entropy
      is a counting argument about microstates, not a moral force, and a living body is an open system fed
      by sunlight that holds its order for decades without breaking any law.
      <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

