<!-- ============================== THE LEDGER ============================== -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">The Ledger</p>
    <h2 id="t-what-holds-up-and-what-does-not">What Holds Up, and What Does Not</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Survives</h3>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>S = k log W.</strong> Entropy is a count of microstates, and the second law follows from there being more of some than of others.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>Information is physical.</strong> Landauer's <em>kT</em>&nbsp;ln&nbsp;2 per bit erased, measured by B&eacute;rut and colleagues in 2012.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>Phases are broken symmetries.</strong> Landau, Wilson, Kosterlitz and Thouless; universality is measured, not asserted.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>Objectivity comes from redundancy.</strong> Zurek's einselection and quantum Darwinism &mdash; the honest version of "existence is what is recorded".</li>
        <li><span class="hist">&#9670;</span> <strong>666 was a name.</strong> Gematria for Neron Kesar, with 616 in the manuscripts to prove it.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">&#9670;</span> <strong>666 is the sum of the squares of the first seven primes.</strong> Checked, and true.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Does Not Survive</h3>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>"Phases of matter are phases of integration."</strong> A re-description, not a theory; it yields no exponent, no transition temperature, no number at all.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>"Polarity accumulates and that is electromagnetism."</strong> Charge does not accumulate, does not vary with history, and is exactly symmetric between proton and electron.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>"The poles stand at 101 and 666."</strong> Base-ten artefacts, and 666 is not even prime.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">&#9670;</span> <strong>"Collapse needs an observer."</strong> It does not, and saying so is the oldest mistake in the subject.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">&#9670;</span> <strong>Any prediction from the doctrine.</strong> There is none yet. Until there is, it is myth, and it is filed as myth.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

