<!-- ============================== GLOSSARY ================================ -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2 id="t-the-words">The Words</h2>
    <dl class="glossary">
      <dt>Entropy</dt><dd>The logarithm of the number of microscopic arrangements consistent with what you know about a system. Not disorder, and not decay.</dd>
      <dt>Microstate, macrostate</dt><dd>The exact arrangement, and the coarse description it satisfies. Entropy is the bridge between them.</dd>
      <dt>The past hypothesis</dt><dd>The assumption, needed to make the second law work, that the universe began in a state of extremely low entropy.</dd>
      <dt>Order parameter</dt><dd>A quantity that is zero in one phase and non-zero in another &mdash; magnetisation, density difference, the condensate wavefunction. The measure of a broken symmetry.</dd>
      <dt>Universality class</dt><dd>The set of utterly different systems that behave identically near a critical point. The reason a magnet and a fluid share numbers.</dd>
      <dt>Landauer's limit</dt><dd><em>kT</em>&nbsp;ln&nbsp;2 of heat per bit erased. The price of forgetting, in joules.</dd>
      <dt>Einselection</dt><dd>Environment-induced superselection: the environment picks out which states survive decoherence, and those are the ones that look classical.</dd>
      <dt>Quantum Darwinism</dt><dd>Zurek's account of objectivity: a fact is objective when the environment holds many redundant copies of it.</dd>
      <dt>Positive polarisation</dt><dd>In the Law of One material, the path of service to others, as against service to self. Primary esoteric text, used here as such.</dd>
      <dt>Collapsed memory</dt><dd>The order's phrase for the single surviving history after decoherence &mdash; what the universe has actually kept.</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

